{"recall":{"defs":[["Convolution (DL)","Cross-correlation of input with a learned kernel."],["Feature map","Output of one filter over the input."],["Receptive field","Input region affecting a neuron."],["Padding / stride","Border zeros / step size."],["Dilation","Gaps between kernel taps."],["Pooling","Parameter-free downsampling (max/avg)."],["1×1 convolution","Per-pixel channel mixing."],["GAP","Average each channel to one number."],["Residual block","y = F(x) + x."],["Transfer learning","Reuse a pre-trained network."]],"formulas":["(I\\star K)(i,j)=\\sum_m\\sum_nI(i+m,j+n)K(m,n)","O=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n+2p-k}{s}\\right\\rfloor+1","\\text{params}=(k^2C_{in}+1)C_{out}","RF_l=RF_{l-1}+(k_l-1)\\prod_{i<l}s_i","k_{eff}=k+(k-1)(r-1)","p_{same}=(k-1)/2","\\mathbf y=F(\\mathbf x)+\\mathbf x,\\ \\ \\frac{\\partial\\mathcal L}{\\partial\\mathbf x}=\\frac{\\partial\\mathcal L}{\\partial\\mathbf y}(1+\\frac{\\partial F}{\\partial\\mathbf x})"],"takeaways":["Local connectivity + weight sharing + equivariance.","Stack conv–ReLU–pool: size ↓, channels ↑, receptive field ↑.","Parameters don't depend on image size; pooling has none.","1×1 bottlenecks and multi-scale modules for efficiency; residuals for depth.","Fine-tune pre-trained networks; augment and regularise."],"confused":[["Convolution vs cross-correlation","DL frameworks don't flip the kernel."],["Equivariance vs invariance","Output shifts with input vs output unchanged."],["Strided vs dilated","Downsamples vs keeps resolution with bigger RF."],["Max vs average pooling","Strongest activation vs smooth mean."],["Feature extraction vs fine-tuning","Frozen backbone vs all layers trained (small η)."]],"minute":"A CNN applies small learned kernels across an image: each output is Σ I(i+m, j+n)K(m, n) + b, one filter gives one feature map, and the same weights are reused at every position. Output size is ⌊(n + 2p − k)/s⌋ + 1; same padding uses p = (k − 1)/2; dilation enlarges the receptive field to k + (k − 1)(r − 1) with the same weights. Filters span all input channels, so a layer has (k²C_in + 1)C_out parameters; pooling has none. Stacks of conv–ReLU–pool reduce spatial size and increase channels; receptive fields grow 3, 5, 7, 9 for stacked 3×3 layers. 1×1 convolutions mix channels and create bottlenecks (Inception: 390M → 118M operations). ResNet's y = F(x) + x keeps gradients flowing through 100+ layers. In practice, start from a pre-trained network: feature extraction for small similar data, fine-tuning for more data."},"flashcards":[["Three key principles of CNNs","Local connectivity, parameter sharing, equivariant representations"],["Architecture pattern","INPUT → [CONV → ACT → POOL] × N → FC → OUTPUT"],["Cross-correlation","$\\sum_m\\sum_nI(i+m,j+n)K(m,n)$"],["Feature map","Output of one filter; high where its pattern appears"],["64 filters of 3×3 on 32×32×3","Output 30×30×64; 1,792 parameters"],["Receptive-field formula","$RF_l=RF_{l-1}+(K_l-1)\\prod S_i$"],["Parameters per filter","$K\\times K\\times C_{in}+1$ (577 for 3×3×64)"],["Same padding (stride 1)","$p=(k-1)/2$"],["Output size","$\\lfloor(n+2p-k)/s\\rfloor+1$"],["Dilated kernel effective size","$k+(k-1)(r-1)$; 3×3, r=2 → 5×5"],["Pooling example max / avg","(6, 9; 7, 8) / (4.5, 7; 4.75, 5)"],["1×1 convolution","Weighted sum across channels at each pixel"],["Conv layer parameters","$(K\\cdot K\\cdot C_{in}+1)\\cdot C_{out}$; 4,864 for 5×5, 3→64"],["ResNet bottleneck savings","≈70K vs ≈590K parameters (≈8.5×)"],["AlexNet","8 layers, 60M params, ReLU, dropout, GPUs; 15.3% top-5 (2012)"],["VGG-16","13 conv + 3 FC, all 3×3; 138M params"],["Global average pooling","$\\frac1{HW}\\sum_{i,j}F_c(i,j)$ per channel; no parameters"],["Inception savings","≈390M → ≈118M operations (3.3×)"],["Residual learning","$H(\\mathbf x)=F(\\mathbf x)+\\mathbf x$"],["Transfer strategy: small & similar data","Feature extraction (freeze, train classifier)"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what","why","h1"],"deep":["c6-what","c6-why","c6-princi